{# The two scoped bots. A scoped bot carries only a `scope` — its permissions come from the
   scoped_role_assignment in 3-assignments.yaml, and `tctl bots add` cannot create one, so
   these are resources rather than `bots:` manifest entries.

   Two bots because each joins with its OWN bound_keypair token: such a token binds a single
   keypair to a single bot (`spec.bot`), so the positive bot and the out-of-scope-app
   negative cannot share one. #}
kind: bot
version: v1
metadata:
  name: app-bot
spec: {}
scope: "{{ scope }}"
---
{# Same shape; this one deliberately asks for an app that only exists OUTSIDE the scope. #}
kind: bot
version: v1
metadata:
  name: nf-bot
spec: {}
scope: "{{ scope }}"
